{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^### (class CharacterController|interface CharacterOptions|class Vehicle|interface VehicleOptions|class Terrain|interface TerrainOptions|class GrassField|interface GrassOptions|class SpriteBatch|class Rng|interface ClipDef|interface RigSpec)'\"' API.md && sed -n '1510,1595p' API.md && sed -n '2024,2079p' API.md && sed -n '2582,2624p' API.md && sed -n '4298,4345p' API.md && sed -n '4836,4896p' API.md && sed -n '3539,3608p' API.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n '\"'^### (class CharacterController|interface CharacterOptions|class Vehicle|interface VehicleOptions|class Terrain|interface TerrainOptions|class GrassField|interface GrassOptions|class SpriteBatch|class Rng|interface ClipDef|interface RigSpec)'\"' API.md && sed -n '1510,1595p' API.md && sed -n '2024,2079p' API.md && sed -n '2582,2624p' API.md && sed -n '4298,4345p' API.md && sed -n '4836,4896p' API.md && sed -n '3539,3608p' API.md\"","aggregated_output":"1476:### class CharacterController\n1500:### interface CharacterOptions\n2024:### class Vehicle\n2042:### interface VehicleOptions\n3547:### interface ClipDef\n3764:### interface RigSpec\n4300:### class GrassField\n4310:### interface GrassOptions\n4651:### class Rng\n4780:### class SpriteBatch\n4836:### class Terrain\n4872:### interface TerrainOptions\n\nBreaking a box into pieces: cut planes along each axis at jittered positions, so the\nchunks tile the box exactly (nothing missing, nothing overlapping) but look hand-broken,\nnot like a grid. Pure and seeded (the same box breaks the same way every time).\n\n  const chunks = fractureBox([2, 3, 0.4], { cuts: [3, 4, 1], jitter: 0.35, seed: 7 });\n  // [{ center: [x, y, z], size: [w, h, d] }, ...] in the box's own space\n\n- `readonly center: [number, number, number]`: Centre in the box's local space (the box is centred on the origin).\n- `readonly size: [number, number, number]`\n\n### clothGrid()\n\n```ts\nfunction clothGrid(o: ClothOptions): VerletBody & { cols: number; rows: number; uv: Float32Array }\n```\n\nA sheet of cloth: a grid of particles with structural, shear and bend edges, two triangles per cell.\n\n### interface ClothOptions\n\n- `width: number`\n- `height: number`\n- `cols: number`: Particles across and down (≥ 2).\n- `rows: number`\n- `origin: readonly [number, number, number]`: The top-left corner. The cloth lies in the plane spanned by `across` and `down`.\n- `across?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Direction along the top edge (unit). Default +X.\n- `down?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Direction from the top edge to the bottom one (unit). Default −Y (hanging); +Z lays it flat.\n- `pin?: 'top' | 'corners' | 'left' | 'none'`: Pinned particles: the whole top edge, its two corners, the left edge (a flag), or none.\n- `shear?: number`: Shear and bend springs (0..1 stiffness). Default 0.8 / 0.3.\n- `bend?: number`\n- `iterations?: number`\n\n### interface Crumble\n\n- `readonly o: CrumbleOptions`\n- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\n- `collider: RAPIER.Collider | null`\n- `state: 'solid' | 'shaking' | 'falling'`: 'solid' → 'shaking' → 'falling' → (regrow) 'solid'.\n- `t: number`\n\n### interface CrumbleOptions\n\n- `at: Vec3`\n- `size: Vec3`\n- `color: PaletteColor`\n- `delay?: number`: Seconds standing on it before it drops (it shakes meanwhile). Default 0.6.\n- `regrow?: number`: Seconds until it grows back (0: never). Default 5.\n\n### interface DoorOptions\n\n- `width?: number`\n- `height?: number`\n- `thickness?: number`\n- `swing?: number`: Swing limit either way (degrees). Default 110.\n- `yaw?: number`: Turn the door frame about Y (radians).\n- `color?: PaletteColor`\n- `closing?: number`: A spring that swings it shut again (stiffness per unit inertia, 0: none). Default 4.\n\n### interface DriveInput\n\n- `throttle: number`: -1 (reverse) … 1\n- `steer: number`: -1 (left) … 1 (right)\n- `brake?: boolean`\n- `handbrake?: boolean`\n\n### explode()\n\n```ts\nfunction explode(world: RAPIER_TYPE.World, at: Vec3, o: ExplosionOptions = {}): number\n```\n\nPush every dynamic body within `radius` of `at` away from it (a speed change, so light and\nheavy things fly alike). Returns how many were hit.\n\n### interface ExplosionOptions\n\n- `radius?: number`\n- `impulse?: number`: Speed change (m/s) at the centre, fading to 0 at the radius. Default 10.\n- `up?: number`: Extra upward share (0..1): blasts throw things up. Default 0.4.\n\n### interface Field\n\n- `enabled: boolean`\n- `remove(): void`: Stop and forget it.\n\n### class Vehicle\n\n- `new Vehicle(physics: Physics, o: VehicleOptions)`\n- `readonly body: RAPIER.RigidBody`\n- `readonly controller: RAPIER.DynamicRayCastVehicleController`\n- `readonly o: Required<Omit<VehicleOptions, 'at' | 'yaw'>>`\n- `readonly mounts: [number, number, number][]`: Wheels' chassis-space mount points (front left, front right, rear left, rear right).\n- `steering: number`: Smoothed steering (-1..1).\n- `slip: number`: How fast the car slides sideways (m/s), and the angle between where it points and where it goes (radians): drifting when high.\n- `slipAngle: number`\n- `setSuspension(stiffness: number): void`: Spring stiffness of every wheel's suspension (live).\n- `get speed: number`: Speed along the car's heading (m/s, negative reversing). Not Rapier's `currentVehicleSpeed`, which counts the up-and-down too (the suspension holding the body up against gravity every step reads as a crawl when parked).\n- `drive(input: DriveInput, dt: number): void`: One fixed step of driving.\n- `wheelPose(i: number, pos: Vector3, rot: Quaternion, local = false): void`: Where wheel `i` is drawn: on its suspension, turned by steering and spin. In the world, or with `local` in the chassis' own space (a wheel mesh parented to a chassis mesh that a physics binding draws between steps).\n- `get yaw: number`: The chassis' heading (radians about Y; 0 drives toward +Z).\n- `reset(at: readonly [number, number, number], yaw = 0): void`: Put it back on its wheels at `at` (a reset after a roll).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### interface VehicleOptions\n\n- `at: readonly [number, number, number]`\n- `yaw?: number`: Heading (radians about Y; 0 drives toward +Z).\n- `size?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Chassis half extents (m). Default [0.9, 0.35, 1.8].\n- `mass?: number`: Chassis mass in world units. Default 8.\n- `wheelRadius?: number`\n- `suspension?: number`: Suspension rest length and stiffness.\n- `stiffness?: number`\n- `power?: number`: Forward drive force per driven wheel at full throttle. Default 30.\n- `topSpeed?: number`: The engine gives out toward this speed (m/s). Default 16.\n- `steer?: number`: Most steering angle (radians). Default 0.55.\n- `grip?: number`: Grip (friction slip): how much sideways force the tyres hold before sliding. Default 2.2.\n- `driftYaw?: number`: Most spin (rad/s) the handbrake's drift push builds up. Default 2.4; 0 turns the assist off.\n\n### class VerletBody\n\n- `new VerletBody(count: number, o: VerletOptions = {})`\n- `readonly count: number`\n- `readonly pos: Float32Array`: Positions, xyz per particle.\n- `readonly prev: Float32Array`: Last step's positions (velocity = pos − prev).\n- `readonly invMass: Float32Array`: 0 for pinned particles.\n- `readonly pinAt: Float32Array`: Where pinned particles are held (move them to drag a cloth by its corner).\n- `ea: Uint32Array<ArrayBuffer>`: Distance constraints: particle pairs, rest lengths and stiffness 0..1.\n- `eb: Uint32Array<ArrayBuffer>`\n- `rest: Float32Array<ArrayBuffer>`\n- `stiff: Float32Array<ArrayBuffer>`\n- `tris: Uint32Array<ArrayBuffer>`: Triangles (cloth and blobs): wind drag, volume and drawing.\n- `gravity: [number, number, number]`\n- `wind: [number, number, number]`: Wind velocity (m/s): drags triangles (by their facing) or particles (ropes).\n- `gust: number`: How much the wind varies in time and space (0..1).\n- `drag: number`: How hard the wind pushes. Cloth: acceleration per (m/s)² of wind hitting it squarely (light cloth: high; canvas: low). Ropes: per m/s of speed relative to the wind.\n- `skin: number`: Cloth: drag along its surface, as a share of `drag` (it streams a flag out).\n- `iterations: number`\n- `damping: number`\n- `floor: number | null`: A floor plane every particle stays above (null: none).\n- `friction: number`: Ground friction: how much sideways motion a particle on the floor keeps.\n- `readonly spheres: Sphere[]`\n### interface Song\n\nA chiptune song as data. Each pattern holds one string per track: space-separated steps,\nwhere a step is a note ('C4', 'F#5', 'Bb2'), '.' (rest) or '-' (hold the previous note).\nEvery track of a pattern must have the same number of steps. For `noise` tracks the\nnote's pitch is the noise rate: C6 is a snare-ish hiss, C8 a hi-hat tick.\n\n- `bpm: number`\n- `stepsPerBeat?: number`: Steps per beat (4 = sixteenth notes). Default 4.\n- `tracks: Record<string, Instrument>`\n- `patterns: Record<string, Record<string, string>>`\n- `order: readonly string[]`: Pattern names in play order.\n- `loop?: boolean`: Loop forever (default true).\n\n### interface SoundDef\n\n- `wave: Wave`\n- `freq: number`: Start pitch in Hz. For `noise` it is the sample-and-hold rate (higher = hissier).\n- `freqEnd?: number`: End pitch for a sweep (exponential glide from `freq`).\n- `sweepTime?: number`: Seconds the sweep takes (default: the whole sound).\n- `duty?: number`: Square duty cycle: 0.125, 0.25 or 0.5 are the classic NES widths. Default 0.5.\n- `attack?: number`: Envelope (seconds): ramp up, hold at full volume, then fade out.\n- `sustain?: number`\n- `decay?: number`\n- `volume?: number`: Peak level 0..1 (default 0.5).\n- `arp?: readonly number[]`: Arpeggio: semitone offsets stepped every `arpRate` seconds (the coin \"ba-ding\").\n- `arpRate?: number`\n- `vibrato?: { depth: number; rate: number }`: Vibrato depth in semitones and rate in Hz.\n- `crush?: number`: Quantize to this many levels (4-bit style crunch). 0 = off.\n- `delay?: number`: Seconds of silence before the sound starts (for layers).\n- `layers?: readonly SoundDef[]`: Extra sounds mixed in (e.g. a noise burst under a thump).\n\n### interface Spatial\n\n- `gain: number`: 0..1 volume.\n- `pan: number`: -1 (left) .. 1 (right).\n- `distance: number`\n\n### spatialize()\n\n```ts\nfunction spatialize(listener: Listener, at: V3Like, o: SpatialOptions = {}): Spatial\n```\n- `seed?: number`: Varies the starting layout and the flow. Default: a new one per swarm.\n\n### class GrassField\n\n- `new GrassField(o: GrassOptions)`\n- `readonly wind: Vector2`: Wind along x and z (its length is the strength).\n- `sway: number`: How far blades lean per unit of wind (m at the tip). Default 0.12.\n- `readonly blades: number`: Blades actually placed (the mask can leave fewer than `count`).\n- `push(i: number, at: Vector3Like | null, radius = 0.8): void`: Pusher `i` (0..3): blades within `radius` of `at` part and flatten (radius 0: none).\n- `update(time: number): void`: Per frame (game time).\n- `dispose(): this`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance\n\n### interface GrassOptions\n\n- `area: readonly [number, number]`: Width (x) and depth (z) of the patch, m.\n- `at: readonly [number, number, number]`: Centre of the patch on the ground.\n- `count: number`\n- `height?: readonly [number, number]`: Blade heights (m): shortest and tallest. Default [0.25, 0.55].\n- `width?: number`: Blade width at the root (m). Default 0.07.\n- `base?: number`: Colours (hex): roots and tips.\n- `tip?: number`\n- `mask?: (x: number, z: number) => boolean`: Where blades grow (world x, z); default everywhere in the patch.\n- `ground?: (x: number, z: number) => number`: Ground height under a blade (default: the patch's y).\n- `seed?: number`\n\n### groundFog()\n\n```ts\nfunction groundFog(o: { color?: number; top?: number; amount?: number; near?: number; far?: number } = {}): { node: Node; color: UniformNode<\"color\", Color>; amount: UniformNode<\"float\", number>; top: UniformNode<\"float\", number>; }\n```\n\nFog for `scene.fogNode` with live settings (uniforms: changing them never recompiles):\nground mist that thickens below `top` (m) and a haze that grows with distance from the\ncamera, both up to `amount` (0..1), in `color` (match the sky).\n\n  const mist = groundFog({ color: s.sky, top: 1.5 });\n  (scene as { fogNode: unknown }).fogNode = mist.node;\n  mist.amount.value = 0.8; mist.color.value.setHex(s.sky);\n\n### hashString()\n\n```ts\nfunction hashString(s: string): number\n```\n\nFNV-1a, 32-bit.\n\n### HEADLESS_VIEWPORT\n### class Terrain\n\n- `new Terrain(o: TerrainOptions = {})`\n- `readonly nx: number`\n- `readonly nz: number`\n- `readonly sizeX: number`\n- `readonly sizeZ: number`\n- `readonly at: readonly [number, number, number]`\n- `readonly heights: Float32Array`: Heights at the grid points, row by row along z: `heights[ix + iz * (nx + 1)]`.\n- `readonly mesh: Mesh`\n- `collider: RAPIER.Collider | null`\n- `get cell: [number, number]`: Metres between grid points along x and z.\n- `pointX(ix: number): number`: World x, z of grid point (ix, iz).\n- `pointZ(iz: number): number`\n- `generate(f: (x: number, z: number) => number): this`: Fill the heights from `f(x, z)` (world x, z; metres above the terrain's origin), then redraw.\n- `heightAt(x: number, z: number): number`: Height of the surface at world (x, z), in world y: the triangle it is over, as the mesh and the collider have it. Outside the grid: its nearest edge.\n- `normalAt(x: number, z: number, out = new Vector3()): Vector3`: The surface's normal at world (x, z) (central differences over half a cell).\n- `update(): void`: Redraw the mesh from the heights (positions, flat normals, colours per face).\n- `attach(physics: Physics): RAPIER.Collider`: Make (or remake, after `generate` / `erode`) the heightfield collider: a fixed body at the terrain's origin. Returns it.\n- `detach(): void`: Remove the collider (the mesh stays).\n- `dispose(): void`: The collider and the mesh's geometry go (the shared material stays).\n- `erode(o: ErosionOptions = {}): void`: Hydraulic erosion: `droplets` raindrops, each rolling downhill from a random point. A drop carries soil up to a capacity that grows with its speed, water and how steeply it is falling: below capacity it digs (over a small radius), above it, or going uphill, i…\n\n### TERRAIN_BANDS\n\n```ts\nconst TERRAIN_BANDS: readonly TerrainBand[]\n```\n\nSea, beach, grass, forest, rock, snow (the engine palette).\n\n### interface TerrainBand\n\n- `below: number`: Heights below this (metres above the terrain's origin) take this colour.\n- `color: number`\n\n### interface TerrainOptions\n\n- `size?: readonly [number, number]`: Size in metres along x and z (default [32, 32]).\n- `cells?: readonly [number, number]`: Cells along x and z (default one per metre).\n- `at?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Where the middle of the grid's height 0 is (default the origin).\n- `bands?: readonly TerrainBand[]`: Colour by height, lowest first; the last band takes everything above.\n- `steep?: number`: Faces steeper than this (their normal's y below it) are rock. Default 0.72 (about 44°).\n- `rock?: number`\n\n### class Timeline\n\n- `new Timeline(o: TimelineOptions)`\n- `readonly duration: number`\n- `time: number`: The playhead (s).\n- `playing: boolean`\n- `speed: number`: Playback rate (1: real time, 0.5: slow motion).\n- `ended: boolean`: True once the end has been reached (by playing or skipping).\n- `readonly fired: string[]`: Cue names in the order they fired (tests and tools).\n- `play(): void`\n- `pause(): void`\n- `update(dt: number): void`: Advance by `dt` seconds of game time (times `speed`) while playing, firing the cues passed.\n- `seek(t: number): void`: Move the playhead to `t` without firing the cues in between (scrubbing). Cues before `t` count as done and cues after it will fire again (going back re-arms them). Ignored while skipping (a cue that loops back cannot undo a skip).\n- `skip(): void`: Jump to the end: the cues not yet fired run (except the cosmetic ones), then `onEnd`. Cues after `duration` never fire, played or skipped.\n- `camera(t = this.time): CameraShot | null`: Where the camera is at `t` (default now): on each key at its time, gliding between keys on a smooth curve (Catmull-Rom tangents, so the speed has no jolt at a key; the first and last key of each shot ease in and out). A `cut` key starts a new shot. Null witho…\n- `line(t = this.time): Line | null`: The subtitle showing at `t` (default now), or null.\n## 12. Animation toolkit\n\n### analyzeClip()\n\n```ts\nfunction analyzeClip(model: Object3D, rig: RigSpec, def: ClipDef, clip: AnimationClip): ClipReport\n```\n\n### interface ClipDef\n\n- `name: string`\n- `frames: number`: Length in frames at 30 fps.\n- `loop?: boolean`\n- `keys: readonly Key[]`\n- `layers?: readonly Layer[]`\n- `feet?: readonly FeetKey[]`: Feet track: foot goals interpolated between its own keys and solved with IK every frame, overriding the keyed leg rotations. Use it whenever feet touch the floor through a transition (kneel → stand, sit → lie) so they roll instead of sinking.\n- `speed?: number`: Ground speed (m/s) the clip is authored for at playback rate 1. Locomotion clips set this; metrics then measure foot sliding against it and the runtime can scale playback.\n- `stance?: number`: Gait cycles (gaitClip): the share of the cycle each foot is planted. The right heel strikes at phase 0, the left at 0.5, so the right foot is mid-stance at `stance / 2`.\n- `reach?: number`: Gaits: how far ahead of the hips (m) the middle of the stance is (feet touch down `reach` + half a stance's ground ahead).\n- `grounded?: boolean`: Grounded clip: soles should rest on y = 0 (metrics flag floating / penetration).\n- `fast?: boolean`: Intentionally snappy (flips, punches, launches): skip the angular-speed warning.\n- `notes?: string`\n\n### interface ClipReport\n\nObjective checks for a clip, computed by actually posing the rig (no renderer). These\nare the numbers an agent can't eyeball: foot sliding, ground contact, loop seams,\nvelocity spikes, joint limits. Thresholds are deliberately forgiving; `problems` are\nreal defects, `warnings` are worth a look.\n\n- `name: string`\n- `frames: number`\n- `loop: boolean`\n- `speed: number | null`\n- `minSoleY: number`: Lowest sole point over the clip (m) and the frame it happens. Negative = through the floor.\n- `minSoleFrame: number`\n- `minBodyY: number`: Lowest point of any other body part (knees, hands, head...), where and when.\n- `minBodyMesh: string`\n- `minBodyFrame: number`\n- `floatingFrames: number`: Frames (of grounded clips) where neither sole is within 5 cm of the floor.\n- `footSlide: number`: Mean horizontal slip of the planted foot, m/s (0 = perfectly planted).\n- `loopSeam: number`: Largest joint-angle jump between the last and first frame of a loop, degrees.\n- `maxAngularSpeed: { joint: string; degPerSec: number; frame: number }`: Fastest joint rotation, degrees per second, and where.\n- `limitViolations: { joint: string; axis: 'x' | 'y' | 'z'; frame: number; value: number; range: [number, number] }[]`\n- `pelvisY: [number, number]`: Pelvis height range (m) — how much the body bobs.\n- `problems: string[]`\n- `warnings: string[]`\n\n### compileClip()\n\n```ts\nfunction compileClip(def: ClipDef, rig: RigSpec, rest: RestPose): AnimationClip\n```\n\nBake a ClipDef into a three.js AnimationClip (quaternion + position + scale tracks,\nsampled at 60 Hz so easing and per-axis Euler interpolation — including 360° flips —\nsurvive exactly).\n\n### compileClips()\n\n```ts\nfunction compileClips(defs: readonly ClipDef[], rig: RigSpec, model: Object3D): AnimationClip[]\n```\n\n### interface Foot\n\n- `readonly at: Vec3`: World position of the foot now.\n- `t: number`: Stepping: 0 → 1 through the step; -1 planted.\n- `readonly from: Vec3`\n- `readonly to: Vec3`\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1476,1510p' API.md && sed -n '4651,4698p' API.md && sed -n '4776,4807p' API.md && sed -n '288,322p' API.md && cat index.html\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1476,1510p' API.md && sed -n '4651,4698p' API.md && sed -n '4776,4807p' API.md && sed -n '288,322p' API.md && cat index.html\"","aggregated_output":"### class CharacterController\n\nKinematic capsule driven by Rapier's KinematicCharacterController, with classic\nplatformer affordances (coyote time, jump buffering, variable jump height).\n\nThe body moves in continuous world space; the visual model is interpolated by\nPhysics.bind and only *looks* pixel-aligned through the render pipeline.\n\n- `new CharacterController(physics: Physics, options: CharacterOptions)`\n- `readonly body: RAPIER.RigidBody`\n- `readonly collider: RAPIER.Collider`\n- `readonly controller: RAPIER.KinematicCharacterController`\n- `readonly velocity: Vector3`\n- `grounded: boolean`\n- `facing: number`\n- `get feet: Vector3`: Feet position (bottom of the capsule), continuous world space.\n- `interpolatedFeet(alpha: number): Vector3`: Feet position blended between the previous and current physics step (render use).\n- `setInput(move: Vector3, jumpPressed: boolean, jumpHeld: boolean): void`: Set desired horizontal move direction (world space, length ≤ 1) and jump input.\n- `teleport(position: [number, number, number]): void`\n- `fixedUpdate(dt: number): void`: Call from Physics.update's fixedUpdate callback.\n- `attachAnimations(model: Object3D, clips: readonly AnimationClip[]): void`: Attach a model's animation clips (expects Idle / Walk / Jump).\n- `get animation: CharacterAnim`\n- `updateVisual(model: Object3D, dt: number): void`: Per render frame: pick animation state and advance the mixer.\n\n### interface CharacterOptions\n\n- `position: [number, number, number]`\n- `radius?: number`\n- `halfHeight?: number`: Height of the cylindrical part of the capsule.\n- `speed?: number`\n- `jumpSpeed?: number`\n- `gravity?: number`\n\n### interface Chunk\n\n### class Rng\n\nSeeded randomness. Everything random in a game comes from an `Rng`, so the same seed always\ngives the same result (docs/DOCTRINE.md, principle 1). Each level gets one, `ctx.random`,\nseeded from the engine's seed and the game's name; fork it by purpose so streams stay\nindependent of how many numbers each one drew:\n\n  const level = ctx.random.fork(`level:${n}`);\n  const room = level.fork(`room:${i}`);   // independent of how many numbers `level` drew\n\nNever use Math.random in game or engine code (the lint refuses it).\n\n- `new Rng(seed: number | string)`\n- `get state: number`: The generator's whole state: save it, and set it back to draw the same numbers again.\n- `next(): number`: Uniform in [0, 1). mulberry32.\n- `fork(purpose: string | number): Rng`: A child generator for one purpose; does not advance this one.\n- `range(min: number, max: number): number`: Float in [min, max).\n- `int(min: number, max: number): number`: Integer in [min, max] (inclusive).\n- `chance(p: number): boolean`\n- `pick(items: readonly T[]): T`\n- `weighted(items: readonly T[], weight: (item: T) => number): T`: Pick by weight; entries with weight <= 0 never come up.\n- `shuffle(items: T[]): T[]`\n- `gaussian(mean = 0, sd = 1): number`: Normal distribution (Box–Muller).\n\n### class RopeMesh\n\n- `new RopeMesh(body: VerletBody, material: Material, thickness = 0.06)`\n- `readonly body: VerletBody`\n- `sync(): void`\n\n### SCREEN_LAYER\n\n```ts\nconst SCREEN_LAYER: 2\n```\n\nThe layer for screens and mirrors: drawn by the main camera, never by a RenderView.\n\n### class ScreenFx\n\n- `cover(kind: TransitionKind = 'fade', o: TransitionOptions = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Cover the picture (progress → 1). Resolves when it stops: `true` when it is fully covered, `false` when another transition (or `set`, `clear`) took over first.\n- `reveal(kind?: TransitionKind, o: TransitionOptions = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Uncover it (progress → 0) with `kind` (default: the one that covered it). Resolves like `cover`.\n- `transition(kind: TransitionKind, between: () => unknown, o: TransitionOptions & { revealCenter?: TransitionOptions['center'] } = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Cover, run `between` (load a level, teleport), then reveal, also when `between` throws (the error is passed on). Resolves to whether the cover completed.\n- `set(kind: TransitionKind | null, progress: number): void`: Jump straight to a progress (0 clear, 1 covered), no animation.\n- `flash(color: ScreenColor = 'white', o: FlashOptions = {}): void`: A full-screen flash that fades out.\n- `shockwave(at: Vector3 | readonly [number, number], o: ShockwaveOptions = {}): void`: A ring that pushes the picture outwards from `at` (oldest ring is replaced when 4 run).\n- `clear(): void`: Stop everything (a clear picture).\n- `state(): ScreenFxState`\n- `new SoftMesh(body: VerletBody, material: Material, o: { uv?: Float32Array; doubleSided?: boolean } = {})`\n- `readonly body: VerletBody`\n- `sync(): void`: Copy the particles into the mesh (call once per frame after stepping the body).\n\n### class SpriteBatch\n\n- `new SpriteBatch(sheet: SpriteSheet, o: { capacity: number })`\n- `readonly sheet: SpriteSheet`\n- `spawn(at: readonly [number, number, number], o: SpriteOptions = {}): number`: A new sprite (its index), or -1 when full.\n- `set(i: number, o: SpriteOptions & { at?: readonly [number, number, number] }): void`: Move or change sprite `i`.\n- `put(i: number, x: number, y: number, z: number, frame?: number, flip?: boolean): void`: `set` without the options object, for many sprites every frame: position, then frame and mirror.\n- `at(i: number): [number, number, number]`: Where sprite `i` stands.\n- `frameOf(i: number): number`: The frame sprite `i` shows.\n- `dispose(): this`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance\n\n### interface SpriteOptions\n\n- `size?: number`: Height in metres (the width follows the frame's aspect). Default 1.\n- `frame?: number`\n- `flip?: boolean`: Mirror left-right (a sprite facing the other way).\n\n### interface SpriteSheet\n\n- `readonly texture: Texture`: The sheet (nearest-filtered); `drawSheet` makes one from code. Frames run left to right, top to bottom, from the image's top-left; a texture with `flipY` false (a `DataTexture`) holds its rows top line first.\n- `readonly frame: readonly [number, number]`: Frame size in pixels and the frames across and down.\n- `readonly cols: number`\n- `readonly rows: number`\n- `readonly frames: number`\n\n### swayMaterial()\n\n```ts\n### interface GameContext\n\n- `readonly engine: Engine`\n- `readonly scene: Scene`\n- `readonly physics: Physics`\n- `readonly input: Input`\n- `readonly camera: CameraRig`\n- `readonly loadModel: typeof loadModel`\n- `readonly palette: typeof PALETTE`\n- `readonly time: number`: Game time in seconds since start. Frozen while paused or loading.\n- `readonly random: Rng`: This level's seeded randomness (src/engine/random.ts): the same engine seed and game give the same numbers. Use it (or forks of it) for everything random; never Math.random.\n- `readonly audio: AudioManager`: Sound effects, music, volumes (src/engine/audio).\n- `readonly particles: Particles`: Pixel particles: `particles.burst('dust', at)` (src/engine/particles).\n- `readonly hud: Hud`: Pixel HUD text and icons in art pixels (src/engine/hud).\n- `readonly lights: LightPool`: Dynamic point lights: `lights.request({ position, color, intensity, radius, flicker })` (src/engine/render/lights.ts). A fixed pool sized by quality, created on first use.\n- `readonly tweens: Tweens`: Tweens on game time: `tweens.to(door.position, { y: 3 }, { duration: 0.8, ease: 'outBack' })` (src/engine/tween.ts). Cleared when the level unloads.\n\n### interface HeadlessOptions\n\n`Engine.headless`: the page's options (those about the page do nothing), and where it runs.\n\n- `viewport?: Viewport`: The viewport the art resolution and framing come from, as a page's would (default 960×540 at DPR 1). Pointer aim and HUD layout depend on it: a replay uses its recording's (`Recording.view`).\n- `assets?: AssetReader`: How models and packs are read: `nodeAssets()` (src/engine/node.ts) reads `public/`.\n\n### class LoadingScreen\n\nMinimal pixel-styled loading indicator: a blocky segmented bar and a status word,\nplain DOM (it shows before the renderer exists). Reuses a `.pixel-loading` element\nalready in the container (index.html ships one so it appears before any JS runs).\n\n- `new LoadingScreen(container: HTMLElement, segments = 12)`\n- `readonly root: HTMLElement`\n- `set(progress: number, label?: string): void`: `progress` 0..1; `label` is shown in capitals.\n- `done(): void`\n\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no, viewport-fit=cover\" />\n    <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\" />\n    <title>Pixel Engine game</title>\n    <style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #0d0b14; } #app { position: fixed; inset: 0; }</style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"app\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"./game.js\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > src/core/math.js <<'EOF'\nexport const clamp = (v,a,b)=>Math.max(a,Math.min(b,v));\nexport const lerp = (a,b,t)=>a+(b-a)*t;\nexport const smooth = (a,b,x)=>{const t=clamp((x-a)/(b-a),0,1);return t*t*(3-2*t);};\nexport const dist = (a,b)=>Math.hypot(a.x-b.x,a.z-b.z);\nexport const angle = a=>Math.atan2(Math.sin(a),Math.cos(a));\nexport function segment(x,z,a,b){const dx=b[0]-a[0],dz=b[1]-a[1],t=clamp(((x-a[0])*dx+(z-a[1])*dz)/(dx*dx+dz*dz||1),0,1);return {d:Math.hypot(x-a[0]-dx*t,z-a[1]-dz*t),x:a[0]+dx*t,z:a[1]+dz*t,t};}\nexport function polyDistance(x,z,poly){let best={d:Infinity};for(let i=1;i<poly.length;i++){const p=segment(x,z,poly[i-1],poly[i]);if(p.d<best.d)best=p;}return best;}\nexport const hash = text=>{let h=2166136261;for(const c of String(text)){h\"'^=c.charCodeAt(0);h=Math.imul(h,16777619);}return h>>>0;};\nexport function rle(values){const out=[];let v=values[0],n=0;for(const x of values){if(x!==v){out.push(v,n);v=x;n=0;}n++;}out.push(v,n);return out;}\nexport function unrle(data,target){let i=0;for(let k=0;k<data.length;k+=2){target.fill(data[k],i,i+data[k+1]);i+=data[k+1];}return target;}\nexport const clean = s=>String(s).replace(/[''^a-zA-Z0-9 .,!?'\"':;()\\\\-+/#&]/g,'').slice(0,28);\nEOF\ncat > src/content/tuning-defaults.js <<'EOF'\nexport const SLIDERS = [\n ['playerSpeed','MOVEMENT',1,.5,2,.1],['playerDamageTaken','DAMAGE RECEIVED',1,0,3,.1],['weaponDamage','WEAPON DAMAGE',1,.25,4,.25],['enemyHealth','ENEMY HEALTH',1,.25,4,.25],['enemyAccuracy','ENEMY ACCURACY',1,.25,3,.25],['enemyVision','SIGHT RANGE',90,20,200,5],['enemyReaction','REACTION TIME',.45,.1,2,.05],['wearRate','WEAPON WEAR',1,0,5,.25],['jamRate','JAM CHANCE',1,0,5,.25],['fireSpread','FIRE SPREAD',1,0,3,.1],['fireDamage','FIRE DAMAGE',8,0,30,1],['windEffect','WIND EFFECT',1,0,3,.1],['feverMinutes','FEVER INTERVAL',12,2,40,1],['vehicleTopSpeed','VEHICLE SPEED',26,10,45,1],['vehicleToughness','VEHICLE TOUGHNESS',1,.25,4,.25],['stonesReward','CONTRACT PAY',1,0,5,.25],['buddyWoundChance','RESCUE WOUND RISK',.15,0,1,.05],['dayMinutes','DAY LENGTH',30,2,120,2],['postRemanHours','POST RESET HOURS',24,1,96,1],['regrowHours','REGROWTH HOURS',48,1,200,1]\n];\nexport const DEFAULTS = Object.fromEntries(SLIDERS.map(([id,,v])=>[id,v]));\nexport const makeTuning = ()=>({...DEFAULTS});\nexport const SETTINGS = {music:.1,effects:.8,voices:.75,mouse:1,pad:1.05,invert:false,assist:true,rumble:true,glyphs:'PlayStation',fov:68,subtitles:1,reducedFlashes:false,reducedFever:false,pixels:1,quality:'high'};\nEOF\ncat > src/core/actions.js <<'EOF'\nexport const PAD = {0:'PadCross',1:'PadCircle',2:'PadSquare',3:'PadTriangle',4:'PadL1',5:'PadR1',6:'PadL2',7:'PadR2',8:'PadCreate',9:'PadOptions',10:'PadL3',11:'PadR3',12:'PadUp',13:'PadDown',14:'PadLeft',15:'PadRight'};\nexport const ACTIONS = {fire:['MouseLeft','PadR2'],aim:['MouseRight','PadL2'],use:['KeyE','PadSquare'],reload:['KeyR'],jump:['Space','PadCross'],crouch:['KeyC','PadCircle'],sprint:['ShiftLeft','PadL3'],melee:['KeyF','PadR3'],weapon:['PadTriangle'],throw:['KeyG','PadR1'],heal:['KeyQ','PadL1'],map:['KeyM','Tab','PadUp'],tablet:['KeyH','PadDown'],tracker:['KeyT','PadLeft'],scope:['KeyV','PadRight'],pause:['Escape','PadOptions'],ledger:['KeyJ','PadCreate']};\nexport const down = (i,a)=>i.anyDown(ACTIONS[a]||[a]);\nexport const press = (i,a)=>i.consumeAny(ACTIONS[a]||[a]);\nexport const tapped = (i,a)=>i.wasPressed(...(ACTIONS[a]||[a]));\nexport const KB = {fire:'LMB',aim:'RMB',use:'E',reload:'R',jump:'SPACE',crouch:'C',sprint:'SHIFT',melee:'F',weapon:'1-4',throw:'G',heal:'Q',map:'M',tablet:'H',tracker:'T',scope:'V',pause:'ESC',ledger:'J',confirm:'ENTER',back:'ESC'};\nexport const PS = {fire:'R2',aim:'L2',use:'SQUARE',reload:'SQUARE',jump:'CROSS',crouch:'CIRCLE',sprint:'L3',melee:'R3',weapon:'TRIANGLE',throw:'R1',heal:'L1',map:'UP',tablet:'DOWN',tracker:'LEFT',scope:'RIGHT',pause:'OPTIONS',ledger:'CREATE',confirm:'CROSS',back:'CIRCLE'};\nexport const XB = {fire:'RT',aim:'LT',use:'X',reload:'X',jump:'A',crouch:'B',sprint:'LS',melee:'RS',weapon:'Y',throw:'RB',heal:'LB',map:'UP',tablet:'DOWN',tracker:'LEFT',scope:'RIGHT',pause:'MENU',ledger:'VIEW',confirm:'A',back:'B'};\nexport const keyLabel=(g,a)=>g.device==='pad'?(g.settings.glyphs==='Xbox'?XB:PS)[a]:KB[a];\nEOF\ncat > src/net/session.js <<'EOF'\nimport {Rng} from '../../pixel-engine.js';\nclass Events { handlers={}; on(k,fn){(this.handlers[k]??=[]).push(fn);return ()=>this.handlers[k]=this.handlers[k].filter(f=>f\"'!==fn);} emit(k,...a){for(const fn of this.handlers[k]||[])fn(...a);} }\nexport function hubSession(info){const hub=globalThis.AIHub;return {...info,kind:'\"'hub',time:()=>hub.time(),rng:k=>hub.rng(k),send:(d,o)=>hub.send(d,o),on:(e,f)=>hub.on(e,f),ready:()=>hub.ready(),answer:w=>hub.answer(w),finish:o=>hub.finish(o),fail:m=>hub.fail(m)};}\nexport function soloSession(){const e=new Events(),rng=new Rng(9631);let t=0;return Object.assign(e,{kind:'solo',me:0,host:0,isHost:true,server:false,seed:9631,limitMs:360000,players:[{id:0,name:'ASTER',color:'#e8443a'},{id:1,name:'INES',color:'#3b82f6'},{id:2,name:'DOV',color:'#22c55e'},{id:3,name:'MAGS',color:'#f5b700'}],time:()=>t,advance:dt=>t+=dt*1000,rng:k=>{const r=rng.fork(k);return ()=>r.next();},send:()=>true,ready:()=>{},answer:()=>{},finish:o=>e.emit('end',{reason:'finished',...o}),fail:m=>{throw Error(m);}});}\nexport function linkSession(hosting){const e=new Events(),bc=new BroadcastChannel('hardly-far-cry-link-v1'),start=Date.now();let started=false,roster=[{id:0,name:'ASTER',color:'#e8443a'}];const id=hosting?0:1;const session=Object.assign(e,{kind:'link',me:id,host:0,isHost:hosting,server:false,seed:7613,limitMs:360000,players:roster,time:()=>started?Date.now()-session.startAt:-Infinity,rng:k=>{const r=new Rng('link:'+k);return ()=>r.next();},send:(d,o={})=>{bc.postMessage({type:'data',from:id,data:d,...o});return true;},ready:()=>{if(\"'!hosting)bc.postMessage({type:'\"'join'});},answer:()=>{},begin:()=>{session.startAt=Date.now()+3000;started=true;bc.postMessage({type:'start',at:session.startAt,players:roster});e.emit('start',{});},finish:o=>{bc.postMessage({type:'end',...o});e.emit('end',{reason:'finished',...o});},fail:m=>e.emit('fail',m),dispose:()=>bc.close()});bc.onmessage=({data:m})=>{if(m.type==='join'&&hosting){roster=[roster[0],{id:1,name:'MERCENARY',color:'#3b82f6'}];session.players=roster;bc.postMessage({type:'lobby',players:roster});e.emit('lobby',roster);}if(m.type==='lobby'){session.players=m.players;e.emit('lobby',m.players);}if(m.type==='start'){session.players=m.players;session.startAt=m.at;started=true;e.emit('start',{});}if(m.type==='data'&&(m.to===undefined||m.to===id))e.emit('message',m.data,m.from);if(m.type==='end')e.emit('end',{reason:'finished',...m});};session.created=start;return session;}\nEOF\ncat > src/net/round.js <<'EOF'\nimport {clamp,clean} from '../core/math.js';\nconst SPAWNS=[[-15,-230],[250,-205],[105,-125],[285,-335]];\nconst CASES=[[135,-284],[174,-315],[112,-340],[208,-272],[85,-250],[175,-354]];\nexport class CashRound {\n constructor(game,session){this.game=game;this.session=session;this.players={};this.cases=CASES.map(([x,z],i)=>({id:i,x,z,carrier:-1,banked:false,burned:false}));this.extraction={x:56,z:-190};this.started=session.kind==='solo';this.ended=false;this.seq=0;this.lastAt=-Infinity;this.events=[];this.world=[];this.count=0;this.unsubs=[];this.card={left:10000,ready:[]};for(const p of session.players)this.addPlayer(p);\n this.unsubs.push(session.on('card',c=>this.card=c),session.on('start',()=>{this.started=true;}),session.on('message',(d,from)=>this.message(d,from)),session.on('time-up',()=>{if(session.isHost)this.finish();}),session.on('leave',({id})=>{const p=this.players[id];if(p){this.drop(p);p.left=true;}if(session.isHost&&Object.values(this.players).every(p=>p.left))this.finish();}),session.on('end',o=>{this.ended=true;this.outcome=o;this.game.roundEnded?.(o);this.stop();}));\n }\n addPlayer(info){const [x,z]=SPAWNS[info.id%4];return this.players[info.id]={id:info.id,name:clean(info.name),color:info.color,x,z,yaw:0,pitch:0,hp:100,stones:0,downs:0,revives:0,kills:0,carrying:-1,bleed:0,respawn:0,seq:0,left:false};}\n startNetwork(){if(this.timer||this.session.kind==='solo')return;let n=0;this.timer=setInterval(()=>{if(this.ended)return;this.pump();if(++n%3===0)this.flushWorld();},100);}\n stop(){if(this.timer){clearInterval(this.timer);this.timer=null;}this.game.ctx?.audio.stopMusic();this.game.ctx?.audio.stopLoops();}\n dispose(){this.stop();for(const u of this.unsubs)u?.();this.session.dispose?.();}\n packet(){return {t:'s',at:++this.count,clock:this.session.time(),p:Object.values(this.players).filter(p=>\"'!p.left).map(p=>[p.id,Math.round(p.x*10),Math.round(p.z*10),Math.round(p.yaw*100),Math.round(p.hp),p.stones,p.carrying,p.bleed>0?1:0]),c:this.cases.map(c=>[c.id,Math.round(c.x),Math.round(c.z),c.carrier,c.banked?1:c.burned?2:0])};}\n pump(){const s=this.session;if(this.ended)return;if(s.isHost){s.send(this.packet(),{reliable:false});}else{const p=this.players[s.me];if(p)s.send({t:'\"'me',seq:++this.seq,x:p.x,z:p.z,yaw:p.yaw,pitch:p.pitch},{to:s.host,reliable:false});if(this.events.length)s.send({t:'ev',ev:this.events.splice(0,16)},{to:s.host,reliable:true});}}\n flushWorld(){if(this.session.isHost&&this.world.length){const cells=this.world.splice(0,90);this.session.send({t:'w',ev:cells},{reliable:true});}}\n message(d,from){if(this.ended||\"'!d||typeof d!=='\"'object')return;if(this.session.isHost){const p=this.players[from];if(\"'!p||p.left)return;if(d.t==='\"'me'&&Number.isFinite(d.x)&&Number.isFinite(d.z)&&d.seq>p.seq){p.seq=d.seq;p.x=clamp(d.x,-630,630);p.z=clamp(d.z,-630,630);p.yaw=Number(d.yaw)||0;p.pitch=Number(d.pitch)||0;}if(d.t==='ev'&&Array.isArray(d.ev))for(const ev of d.ev.slice(0,16))this.action(p,ev);}\n else if(d.t==='s'&&d.at>this.lastAt){this.lastAt=d.at;for(const a of d.p){const p=this.players[a[0]];if(\"'!p)continue;if(p.id!==this.session.me){p.x=a[1]/10;p.z=a[2]/10;p.yaw=a[3]/100;}p.hp=a[4];p.stones=a[5];p.carrying=a[6];p.bleed=a[7]?25:0;}for(const a of d.c){const c=this.cases[a[0]];if(c)Object.assign(c,{x:a[1],z:a[2],carrier:a[3],banked:a[4]===1,burned:a[4]===2});}}\n else if(d.t==='\"'w')for(const ev of d.ev){if(ev[0]==='fire')this.game.world?.fire.lightIndex(ev[1]);if(ev[0]==='burnt')this.game.world?.fire.markBurnt(ev[1]);}\n }\n action(p,ev){if(\"'!this.started||this.session.time()<0||p.hp<=0||this.ended)return;if(ev.type==='\"'use'){if(p.carrying>=0&&Math.hypot(p.x-this.extraction.x,p.z-this.extraction.z)<9){const c=this.cases[p.carrying];c.banked=true;c.carrier=-1;p.carrying=-1;p.stones+=5;return;}\n const down=Object.values(this.players).find(q=>q.id\"'!==p.id&&q.bleed>0&&Math.hypot(p.x-q.x,p.z-q.z)<4);if(down&&ev.held>=3){down.hp=45;down.bleed=0;p.revives++;return;}\n const c=this.cases.find(c=>!c.banked&&!c.burned&&c.carrier<0&&Math.hypot(p.x-c.x,p.z-c.z)<5);if(c&&p.carrying<0){c.carrier=p.id;p.carrying=c.id;}}\n if(ev.type==='\"'shot')this.game.resolveRoundShot?.(p,ev);if(ev.type==='ignite')this.game.world?.fire.ignite(ev.x,ev.z,4);}\n local(ev){const p=this.players[this.session.me];if(\"'!p)return;if(this.session.isHost)this.action(p,ev);else this.events.push(ev);}\n drop(p){if(p.carrying>=0){const c=this.cases[p.carrying];c.carrier=-1;c.x=p.x;c.z=p.z;p.carrying=-1;}}\n damage(id,n){const p=this.players[id];if(!p||p.hp<=0)return;p.hp=Math.max(0,p.hp-n);if(p.hp<=0){p.downs++;p.bleed=25;this.drop(p);}}\n tick(dt){if(this.ended||!this.started)return;this.session.advance?.(dt);if(this.session.time()<0)return;for(const p of Object.values(this.players)){if(p.left)continue;if(p.bleed>0){p.bleed-=dt;if(p.bleed<=0)p.respawn=15;}else if(p.respawn>0){p.respawn-=dt;if(p.respawn<=0){const [x,z]=SPAWNS[p.id%4];Object.assign(p,{hp:100,x,z});}}if(p.carrying>=0){const c=this.cases[p.carrying];c.x=p.x;c.z=p.z;}}\n if(this.session.isHost){if(this.session.kind==='\"'solo')this.bots(dt);if(this.session.time()>=this.session.limitMs||this.cases.every(c=>c.banked||c.burned))this.finish();}}\n bots(dt){for(const p of Object.values(this.players)){if(p.id===this.session.me||p.hp<=0)continue;const c=this.cases.filter(c=>\"'!c.banked&&!c.burned&&c.carrier<0).sort((a,b)=>Math.hypot(a.x-p.x,a.z-p.z)-Math.hypot(b.x-p.x,b.z-p.z))[0];const target=p.carrying>=0?this.extraction:c;if(!target)continue;const dx=target.x-p.x,dz=target.z-p.z,d=Math.hypot(dx,dz);p.yaw=Math.atan2(-dx,-dz);if(d>3){p.x+=dx/d*dt*3.9;p.z+=dz/d*dt*3.9;}else this.action(p,{type:'\"'use',held:3});}}\n finish(){if(this.ended||this.finished||\"'!this.session.isHost)return;this.finished=true;const ps=Object.values(this.players).filter(p=>!p.left).sort((a,b)=>b.stones-a.stones),standings=[];for(const p of ps){const last=standings.at(-1);if(last&&this.players[last[0]].stones===p.stones)last.push(p.id);else standings.push([p.id]);}const scores=Object.fromEntries(ps.map(p=>[p.id,p.stones])),stats=Object.fromEntries(ps.map(p=>[p.id,{Stones:p.stones,Downs:p.downs,Revives:p.revives,Kills:p.kills}]));this.session.finish({standings,scores,stats,awards:ps.length?[{id:ps[0].id,title:'\"'Paid in Full',detail:\"'`${ps[0].stones} stones extracted`}]:[]});}\n}\nEOF\ncat > tools/build.mjs <<'\"'EOF'\nimport {execFileSync} from 'node:child_process';\nimport {readFileSync,writeFileSync} from 'node:fs';\nimport {GAME_TITLE} from '../src/content/title.js';\nconst base='Hardly-Far-Cry-Far-Cry-2-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-063014';\nconst bundle=execFileSync('esbuild',['src/main.js','--bundle','--format=esm','--target=esnext','--legal-comments=inline','--log-level=warning'],{maxBuffer:1<<29}).toString();\nconst session=readFileSync('vendor/session.js','utf8');\nconst head=\"'`<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><script>%SESSION%</script>\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\"><meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\"><meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\"><meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Carry the most diamond cases out of the burning mine\"><meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move, R2/mouse fire, Square/E use, carry cases to the truck\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\"><meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#171c22\"><link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\"><title>${GAME_TITLE}</title>\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#131920;overflow:hidden}#app{position:fixed;inset:0}.fallback{position:fixed;inset:0;display:grid;place-content:center;gap:1.3em;padding:8vw;background:#172127;color:#f4d5a2;font:700 clamp(18px,3vw,30px) monospace;line-height:1.5}.fallback h1{color:#ff9a52;font-size:1.5em}.fallback button{font:inherit;background:#eb8c48;color:#172127;border:0;padding:.6em;cursor:pointer}</style></head><body><div id=\"app\"></div><script type=\"module\">%BUNDLE%</script></body></html>`;\nconst html=head.replace('\"'%SESSION%',()=>session.replace(/<\\\\/script/gi,'<\\\\\\\\/script')).replace('%BUNDLE%',()=>bundle.replace(/<\\\\/script/gi,'<\\\\\\\\/script'))+'\\\\n<\"'!--'\"\\\\n'+readFileSync('CREDITS.md','utf8').replace(/-->/g,'-- >')+'\\\\nAI Hub session client 1.4.0. Original game, models, music and text by OpenAI.\\\\n-->\\\\n';\nwriteFileSync('../'+base+'.html',html);\nwriteFileSync('index.html',head.replace('%SESSION%',()=>session).replace('%BUNDLE%','import \\\"./src/main.js\\\";'));\nif(\"'!process.argv.includes('\"'--quiet'))console.log(\"'`${base}.html (${(Buffer.byteLength(html)/1048576).toFixed(2)} MiB)`);\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > src/core/math.js <<'EOF'\nexport const clamp = (v,a,b)=>Math.max(a,Math.min(b,v));\nexport const lerp = (a,b,t)=>a+(b-a)*t;\nexport const smooth = (a,b,x)=>{const t=clamp((x-a)/(b-a),0,1);return t*t*(3-2*t);};\nexport const dist = (a,b)=>Math.hypot(a.x-b.x,a.z-b.z);\nexport const angle = a=>Math.atan2(Math.sin(a),Math.cos(a));\nexport function segment(x,z,a,b){const dx=b[0]-a[0],dz=b[1]-a[1],t=clamp(((x-a[0])*dx+(z-a[1])*dz)/(dx*dx+dz*dz||1),0,1);return {d:Math.hypot(x-a[0]-dx*t,z-a[1]-dz*t),x:a[0]+dx*t,z:a[1]+dz*t,t};}\nexport function polyDistance(x,z,poly){let best={d:Infinity};for(let i=1;i<poly.length;i++){const p=segment(x,z,poly[i-1],poly[i]);if(p.d<best.d)best=p;}return best;}\nexport const hash = text=>{let h=2166136261;for(const c of String(text)){h\"'^=c.charCodeAt(0);h=Math.imul(h,16777619);}return h>>>0;};\nexport function rle(values){const out=[];let v=values[0],n=0;for(const x of values){if(x!==v){out.push(v,n);v=x;n=0;}n++;}out.push(v,n);return out;}\nexport function unrle(data,target){let i=0;for(let k=0;k<data.length;k+=2){target.fill(data[k],i,i+data[k+1]);i+=data[k+1];}return target;}\nexport const clean = s=>String(s).replace(/[''^a-zA-Z0-9 .,!?'\"':;()\\\\-+/#&]/g,'').slice(0,28);\nEOF\ncat > src/content/tuning-defaults.js <<'EOF'\nexport const SLIDERS = [\n ['playerSpeed','MOVEMENT',1,.5,2,.1],['playerDamageTaken','DAMAGE RECEIVED',1,0,3,.1],['weaponDamage','WEAPON DAMAGE',1,.25,4,.25],['enemyHealth','ENEMY HEALTH',1,.25,4,.25],['enemyAccuracy','ENEMY ACCURACY',1,.25,3,.25],['enemyVision','SIGHT RANGE',90,20,200,5],['enemyReaction','REACTION TIME',.45,.1,2,.05],['wearRate','WEAPON WEAR',1,0,5,.25],['jamRate','JAM CHANCE',1,0,5,.25],['fireSpread','FIRE SPREAD',1,0,3,.1],['fireDamage','FIRE DAMAGE',8,0,30,1],['windEffect','WIND EFFECT',1,0,3,.1],['feverMinutes','FEVER INTERVAL',12,2,40,1],['vehicleTopSpeed','VEHICLE SPEED',26,10,45,1],['vehicleToughness','VEHICLE TOUGHNESS',1,.25,4,.25],['stonesReward','CONTRACT PAY',1,0,5,.25],['buddyWoundChance','RESCUE WOUND RISK',.15,0,1,.05],['dayMinutes','DAY LENGTH',30,2,120,2],['postRemanHours','POST RESET HOURS',24,1,96,1],['regrowHours','REGROWTH HOURS',48,1,200,1]\n];\nexport const DEFAULTS = Object.fromEntries(SLIDERS.map(([id,,v])=>[id,v]));\nexport const makeTuning = ()=>({...DEFAULTS});\nexport const SETTINGS = {music:.1,effects:.8,voices:.75,mouse:1,pad:1.05,invert:false,assist:true,rumble:true,glyphs:'PlayStation',fov:68,subtitles:1,reducedFlashes:false,reducedFever:false,pixels:1,quality:'high'};\nEOF\ncat > src/core/actions.js <<'EOF'\nexport const PAD = {0:'PadCross',1:'PadCircle',2:'PadSquare',3:'PadTriangle',4:'PadL1',5:'PadR1',6:'PadL2',7:'PadR2',8:'PadCreate',9:'PadOptions',10:'PadL3',11:'PadR3',12:'PadUp',13:'PadDown',14:'PadLeft',15:'PadRight'};\nexport const ACTIONS = {fire:['MouseLeft','PadR2'],aim:['MouseRight','PadL2'],use:['KeyE','PadSquare'],reload:['KeyR'],jump:['Space','PadCross'],crouch:['KeyC','PadCircle'],sprint:['ShiftLeft','PadL3'],melee:['KeyF','PadR3'],weapon:['PadTriangle'],throw:['KeyG','PadR1'],heal:['KeyQ','PadL1'],map:['KeyM','Tab','PadUp'],tablet:['KeyH','PadDown'],tracker:['KeyT','PadLeft'],scope:['KeyV','PadRight'],pause:['Escape','PadOptions'],ledger:['KeyJ','PadCreate']};\nexport const down = (i,a)=>i.anyDown(ACTIONS[a]||[a]);\nexport const press = (i,a)=>i.consumeAny(ACTIONS[a]||[a]);\nexport const tapped = (i,a)=>i.wasPressed(...(ACTIONS[a]||[a]));\nexport const KB = {fire:'LMB',aim:'RMB',use:'E',reload:'R',jump:'SPACE',crouch:'C',sprint:'SHIFT',melee:'F',weapon:'1-4',throw:'G',heal:'Q',map:'M',tablet:'H',tracker:'T',scope:'V',pause:'ESC',ledger:'J',confirm:'ENTER',back:'ESC'};\nexport const PS = {fire:'R2',aim:'L2',use:'SQUARE',reload:'SQUARE',jump:'CROSS',crouch:'CIRCLE',sprint:'L3',melee:'R3',weapon:'TRIANGLE',throw:'R1',heal:'L1',map:'UP',tablet:'DOWN',tracker:'LEFT',scope:'RIGHT',pause:'OPTIONS',ledger:'CREATE',confirm:'CROSS',back:'CIRCLE'};\nexport const XB = {fire:'RT',aim:'LT',use:'X',reload:'X',jump:'A',crouch:'B',sprint:'LS',melee:'RS',weapon:'Y',throw:'RB',heal:'LB',map:'UP',tablet:'DOWN',tracker:'LEFT',scope:'RIGHT',pause:'MENU',ledger:'VIEW',confirm:'A',back:'B'};\nexport const keyLabel=(g,a)=>g.device==='pad'?(g.settings.glyphs==='Xbox'?XB:PS)[a]:KB[a];\nEOF\ncat > src/net/session.js <<'EOF'\nimport {Rng} from '../../pixel-engine.js';\nclass Events { handlers={}; on(k,fn){(this.handlers[k]??=[]).push(fn);return ()=>this.handlers[k]=this.handlers[k].filter(f=>f\"'!==fn);} emit(k,...a){for(const fn of this.handlers[k]||[])fn(...a);} }\nexport function hubSession(info){const hub=globalThis.AIHub;return {...info,kind:'\"'hub',time:()=>hub.time(),rng:k=>hub.rng(k),send:(d,o)=>hub.send(d,o),on:(e,f)=>hub.on(e,f),ready:()=>hub.ready(),answer:w=>hub.answer(w),finish:o=>hub.finish(o),fail:m=>hub.fail(m)};}\nexport function soloSession(){const e=new Events(),rng=new Rng(9631);let t=0;return Object.assign(e,{kind:'solo',me:0,host:0,isHost:true,server:false,seed:9631,limitMs:360000,players:[{id:0,name:'ASTER',color:'#e8443a'},{id:1,name:'INES',color:'#3b82f6'},{id:2,name:'DOV',color:'#22c55e'},{id:3,name:'MAGS',color:'#f5b700'}],time:()=>t,advance:dt=>t+=dt*1000,rng:k=>{const r=rng.fork(k);return ()=>r.next();},send:()=>true,ready:()=>{},answer:()=>{},finish:o=>e.emit('end',{reason:'finished',...o}),fail:m=>{throw Error(m);}});}\nexport function linkSession(hosting){const e=new Events(),bc=new BroadcastChannel('hardly-far-cry-link-v1'),start=Date.now();let started=false,roster=[{id:0,name:'ASTER',color:'#e8443a'}];const id=hosting?0:1;const session=Object.assign(e,{kind:'link',me:id,host:0,isHost:hosting,server:false,seed:7613,limitMs:360000,players:roster,time:()=>started?Date.now()-session.startAt:-Infinity,rng:k=>{const r=new Rng('link:'+k);return ()=>r.next();},send:(d,o={})=>{bc.postMessage({type:'data',from:id,data:d,...o});return true;},ready:()=>{if(\"'!hosting)bc.postMessage({type:'\"'join'});},answer:()=>{},begin:()=>{session.startAt=Date.now()+3000;started=true;bc.postMessage({type:'start',at:session.startAt,players:roster});e.emit('start',{});},finish:o=>{bc.postMessage({type:'end',...o});e.emit('end',{reason:'finished',...o});},fail:m=>e.emit('fail',m),dispose:()=>bc.close()});bc.onmessage=({data:m})=>{if(m.type==='join'&&hosting){roster=[roster[0],{id:1,name:'MERCENARY',color:'#3b82f6'}];session.players=roster;bc.postMessage({type:'lobby',players:roster});e.emit('lobby',roster);}if(m.type==='lobby'){session.players=m.players;e.emit('lobby',m.players);}if(m.type==='start'){session.players=m.players;session.startAt=m.at;started=true;e.emit('start',{});}if(m.type==='data'&&(m.to===undefined||m.to===id))e.emit('message',m.data,m.from);if(m.type==='end')e.emit('end',{reason:'finished',...m});};session.created=start;return session;}\nEOF\ncat > src/net/round.js <<'EOF'\nimport {clamp,clean} from '../core/math.js';\nconst SPAWNS=[[-15,-230],[250,-205],[105,-125],[285,-335]];\nconst CASES=[[135,-284],[174,-315],[112,-340],[208,-272],[85,-250],[175,-354]];\nexport class CashRound {\n constructor(game,session){this.game=game;this.session=session;this.players={};this.cases=CASES.map(([x,z],i)=>({id:i,x,z,carrier:-1,banked:false,burned:false}));this.extraction={x:56,z:-190};this.started=session.kind==='solo';this.ended=false;this.seq=0;this.lastAt=-Infinity;this.events=[];this.world=[];this.count=0;this.unsubs=[];this.card={left:10000,ready:[]};for(const p of session.players)this.addPlayer(p);\n this.unsubs.push(session.on('card',c=>this.card=c),session.on('start',()=>{this.started=true;}),session.on('message',(d,from)=>this.message(d,from)),session.on('time-up',()=>{if(session.isHost)this.finish();}),session.on('leave',({id})=>{const p=this.players[id];if(p){this.drop(p);p.left=true;}if(session.isHost&&Object.values(this.players).every(p=>p.left))this.finish();}),session.on('end',o=>{this.ended=true;this.outcome=o;this.game.roundEnded?.(o);this.stop();}));\n }\n addPlayer(info){const [x,z]=SPAWNS[info.id%4];return this.players[info.id]={id:info.id,name:clean(info.name),color:info.color,x,z,yaw:0,pitch:0,hp:100,stones:0,downs:0,revives:0,kills:0,carrying:-1,bleed:0,respawn:0,seq:0,left:false};}\n startNetwork(){if(this.timer||this.session.kind==='solo')return;let n=0;this.timer=setInterval(()=>{if(this.ended)return;this.pump();if(++n%3===0)this.flushWorld();},100);}\n stop(){if(this.timer){clearInterval(this.timer);this.timer=null;}this.game.ctx?.audio.stopMusic();this.game.ctx?.audio.stopLoops();}\n dispose(){this.stop();for(const u of this.unsubs)u?.();this.session.dispose?.();}\n packet(){return {t:'s',at:++this.count,clock:this.session.time(),p:Object.values(this.players).filter(p=>\"'!p.left).map(p=>[p.id,Math.round(p.x*10),Math.round(p.z*10),Math.round(p.yaw*100),Math.round(p.hp),p.stones,p.carrying,p.bleed>0?1:0]),c:this.cases.map(c=>[c.id,Math.round(c.x),Math.round(c.z),c.carrier,c.banked?1:c.burned?2:0])};}\n pump(){const s=this.session;if(this.ended)return;if(s.isHost){s.send(this.packet(),{reliable:false});}else{const p=this.players[s.me];if(p)s.send({t:'\"'me',seq:++this.seq,x:p.x,z:p.z,yaw:p.yaw,pitch:p.pitch},{to:s.host,reliable:false});if(this.events.length)s.send({t:'ev',ev:this.events.splice(0,16)},{to:s.host,reliable:true});}}\n flushWorld(){if(this.session.isHost&&this.world.length){const cells=this.world.splice(0,90);this.session.send({t:'w',ev:cells},{reliable:true});}}\n message(d,from){if(this.ended||\"'!d||typeof d!=='\"'object')return;if(this.session.isHost){const p=this.players[from];if(\"'!p||p.left)return;if(d.t==='\"'me'&&Number.isFinite(d.x)&&Number.isFinite(d.z)&&d.seq>p.seq){p.seq=d.seq;p.x=clamp(d.x,-630,630);p.z=clamp(d.z,-630,630);p.yaw=Number(d.yaw)||0;p.pitch=Number(d.pitch)||0;}if(d.t==='ev'&&Array.isArray(d.ev))for(const ev of d.ev.slice(0,16))this.action(p,ev);}\n else if(d.t==='s'&&d.at>this.lastAt){this.lastAt=d.at;for(const a of d.p){const p=this.players[a[0]];if(\"'!p)continue;if(p.id!==this.session.me){p.x=a[1]/10;p.z=a[2]/10;p.yaw=a[3]/100;}p.hp=a[4];p.stones=a[5];p.carrying=a[6];p.bleed=a[7]?25:0;}for(const a of d.c){const c=this.cases[a[0]];if(c)Object.assign(c,{x:a[1],z:a[2],carrier:a[3],banked:a[4]===1,burned:a[4]===2});}}\n else if(d.t==='\"'w')for(const ev of d.ev){if(ev[0]==='fire')this.game.world?.fire.lightIndex(ev[1]);if(ev[0]==='burnt')this.game.world?.fire.markBurnt(ev[1]);}\n }\n action(p,ev){if(\"'!this.started||this.session.time()<0||p.hp<=0||this.ended)return;if(ev.type==='\"'use'){if(p.carrying>=0&&Math.hypot(p.x-this.extraction.x,p.z-this.extraction.z)<9){const c=this.cases[p.carrying];c.banked=true;c.carrier=-1;p.carrying=-1;p.stones+=5;return;}\n const down=Object.values(this.players).find(q=>q.id\"'!==p.id&&q.bleed>0&&Math.hypot(p.x-q.x,p.z-q.z)<4);if(down&&ev.held>=3){down.hp=45;down.bleed=0;p.revives++;return;}\n const c=this.cases.find(c=>!c.banked&&!c.burned&&c.carrier<0&&Math.hypot(p.x-c.x,p.z-c.z)<5);if(c&&p.carrying<0){c.carrier=p.id;p.carrying=c.id;}}\n if(ev.type==='\"'shot')this.game.resolveRoundShot?.(p,ev);if(ev.type==='ignite')this.game.world?.fire.ignite(ev.x,ev.z,4);}\n local(ev){const p=this.players[this.session.me];if(\"'!p)return;if(this.session.isHost)this.action(p,ev);else this.events.push(ev);}\n drop(p){if(p.carrying>=0){const c=this.cases[p.carrying];c.carrier=-1;c.x=p.x;c.z=p.z;p.carrying=-1;}}\n damage(id,n){const p=this.players[id];if(!p||p.hp<=0)return;p.hp=Math.max(0,p.hp-n);if(p.hp<=0){p.downs++;p.bleed=25;this.drop(p);}}\n tick(dt){if(this.ended||!this.started)return;this.session.advance?.(dt);if(this.session.time()<0)return;for(const p of Object.values(this.players)){if(p.left)continue;if(p.bleed>0){p.bleed-=dt;if(p.bleed<=0)p.respawn=15;}else if(p.respawn>0){p.respawn-=dt;if(p.respawn<=0){const [x,z]=SPAWNS[p.id%4];Object.assign(p,{hp:100,x,z});}}if(p.carrying>=0){const c=this.cases[p.carrying];c.x=p.x;c.z=p.z;}}\n if(this.session.isHost){if(this.session.kind==='\"'solo')this.bots(dt);if(this.session.time()>=this.session.limitMs||this.cases.every(c=>c.banked||c.burned))this.finish();}}\n bots(dt){for(const p of Object.values(this.players)){if(p.id===this.session.me||p.hp<=0)continue;const c=this.cases.filter(c=>\"'!c.banked&&!c.burned&&c.carrier<0).sort((a,b)=>Math.hypot(a.x-p.x,a.z-p.z)-Math.hypot(b.x-p.x,b.z-p.z))[0];const target=p.carrying>=0?this.extraction:c;if(!target)continue;const dx=target.x-p.x,dz=target.z-p.z,d=Math.hypot(dx,dz);p.yaw=Math.atan2(-dx,-dz);if(d>3){p.x+=dx/d*dt*3.9;p.z+=dz/d*dt*3.9;}else this.action(p,{type:'\"'use',held:3});}}\n finish(){if(this.ended||this.finished||\"'!this.session.isHost)return;this.finished=true;const ps=Object.values(this.players).filter(p=>!p.left).sort((a,b)=>b.stones-a.stones),standings=[];for(const p of ps){const last=standings.at(-1);if(last&&this.players[last[0]].stones===p.stones)last.push(p.id);else standings.push([p.id]);}const scores=Object.fromEntries(ps.map(p=>[p.id,p.stones])),stats=Object.fromEntries(ps.map(p=>[p.id,{Stones:p.stones,Downs:p.downs,Revives:p.revives,Kills:p.kills}]));this.session.finish({standings,scores,stats,awards:ps.length?[{id:ps[0].id,title:'\"'Paid in Full',detail:\"'`${ps[0].stones} stones extracted`}]:[]});}\n}\nEOF\ncat > tools/build.mjs <<'\"'EOF'\nimport {execFileSync} from 'node:child_process';\nimport {readFileSync,writeFileSync} from 'node:fs';\nimport {GAME_TITLE} from '../src/content/title.js';\nconst base='Hardly-Far-Cry-Far-Cry-2-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-063014';\nconst bundle=execFileSync('esbuild',['src/main.js','--bundle','--format=esm','--target=esnext','--legal-comments=inline','--log-level=warning'],{maxBuffer:1<<29}).toString();\nconst session=readFileSync('vendor/session.js','utf8');\nconst head=\"'`<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><script>%SESSION%</script>\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\"><meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\"><meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\"><meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"6\"><meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\"><meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Carry the most diamond cases out of the burning mine\"><meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move, R2/mouse fire, Square/E use, carry cases to the truck\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\"><meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#171c22\"><link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\"><title>${GAME_TITLE}</title>\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#131920;overflow:hidden}#app{position:fixed;inset:0}.fallback{position:fixed;inset:0;display:grid;place-content:center;gap:1.3em;padding:8vw;background:#172127;color:#f4d5a2;font:700 clamp(18px,3vw,30px) monospace;line-height:1.5}.fallback h1{color:#ff9a52;font-size:1.5em}.fallback button{font:inherit;background:#eb8c48;color:#172127;border:0;padding:.6em;cursor:pointer}</style></head><body><div id=\"app\"></div><script type=\"module\">%BUNDLE%</script></body></html>`;\nconst html=head.replace('\"'%SESSION%',()=>session.replace(/<\\\\/script/gi,'<\\\\\\\\/script')).replace('%BUNDLE%',()=>bundle.replace(/<\\\\/script/gi,'<\\\\\\\\/script'))+'\\\\n<\"'!--'\"\\\\n'+readFileSync('CREDITS.md','utf8').replace(/-->/g,'-- >')+'\\\\nAI Hub session client 1.4.0. Original game, models, music and text by OpenAI.\\\\n-->\\\\n';\nwriteFileSync('../'+base+'.html',html);\nwriteFileSync('index.html',head.replace('%SESSION%',()=>session).replace('%BUNDLE%','import \\\"./src/main.js\\\";'));\nif(\"'!process.argv.includes('\"'--quiet'))console.log(\"'`${base}.html (${(Buffer.byteLength(html)/1048576).toFixed(2)} MiB)`);\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"The project structure and shared-world Cash Run rules are in place. I’m checking the single-file build and hub handshake early, then I’ll build the terrain, combat, and story on that foundation."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > src/core/look.js <<'EOF'\nexport const LOOK={scene:[{id:'adjust',params:{brightness:0,contrast:1.06,saturation:1.05,warmth:.04}},{id:'chromatic',params:{spread:0}},{id:'vignette',params:{intensity:.28,softness:.7,amount:1}}],actors:{pixel:{size:1,outline:.45,crease:.08},filters:[]},environment:{pixel:{size:1,outline:.32,crease:.05},filters:[]}};\nexport function installLook(g,ctx){const rig=ctx.camera;rig.camera.far=1100;rig.camera.near=.05;rig.camera.updateProjectionMatrix();rig.step=function(u){if(g.cam.override){this.camera.position.set(...g.cam.override.position);this.camera.lookAt(...g.cam.override.target);this.focus.copy(this.camera.position);return;}const k=g.cam.enabled?1:0,s=g.device==='pad'?g.settings.pad:g.settings.mouse;this.yaw-=u.input.mouseDelta.x*.0025*s*k;this.pitch=Math.max(-1.4,Math.min(1.4,this.pitch-u.input.mouseDelta.y*.0025*s*(g.settings.invert?-1:1)*k));this.focus.copy(u.target);this.camera.position.copy(u.eye);this.camera.rotation.set(this.pitch,this.yaw,0);};}\nEOF\ncat > src/game.js <<'EOF'\nimport {THREE,toonMaterial,applySky,skyAt} from '../pixel-engine.js';\nimport {GAME_TITLE} from './content/title.js';\nimport {PAD} from './core/actions.js';\nimport {SETTINGS,makeTuning} from './content/tuning-defaults.js';\nimport {installLook} from './core/look.js';\nimport {CashRound} from './net/round.js';\nexport class SorrelGame {\n name=GAME_TITLE; assets=[];\n constructor(options={}){this.options=options;this.mode=options.session?'round':'title';this.screen=options.session?'card':'title';this.settings={...SETTINGS};this.tuning=makeTuning();this.device='kbm';this.focus=0;this.cam={override:null,enabled:false};this.pos=new THREE.Vector3(0,40,20);this.eye=new THREE.Vector3();this.hp=100;this.stones=0;this.tablets=3;this.syrettes=3;this.hour=16.5;this.wind={x:-.8,z:-.6,speed:5};this.prompts=[];this.idle=0;this.notice=options.touch?'Controller or keyboard required':'';if(options.session)this.round=new CashRound(this,options.session);}\n setup(ctx){this.ctx=ctx;ctx.input.gamepadButtons={...PAD};Object.defineProperty(ctx.input,'wantsPointerLock',{get:()=>false,set(){},configurable:true});installLook(this,ctx);const floor=new THREE.Mesh(new THREE.PlaneGeometry(1280,1280),toonMaterial(ctx.palette.sand));floor.rotation.x=-Math.PI/2;floor.position.y=40;ctx.scene.add(floor);ctx.physics.addStaticBox({position:[0,39,0],halfExtents:[640,1,640]});applySky(ctx.engine,skyAt(16.5));ctx.audio.setVolume('music',.1);this.cam.override={position:[0,45,26],target:[0,40,0]};}\n ready(ctx){if(typeof window\"'!=='\"'undefined')window.__GAME__=this;this.round?.startNetwork();this.options.session?.ready();}\n fixedUpdate(ctx,dt){this.round?.tick(dt);}\n update(ctx,dt){const h=ctx.hud;h.clear();if(this.round){if(this.round.started&&this.screen==='card')this.screen='';if(this.screen==='card'){h.rect(18,26,h.width-36,204,'ink');h.text(32,40,GAME_TITLE,{scale:3,color:'orange'});h.text(32,82,'CASH RUN / 6 MINUTES',{scale:2});h.text(32,111,'CARRY CASES TO THE EXTRACTION TRUCK.');for(const [j,p] of Object.values(this.round.players).entries())h.text(32,132+j*14,p.name+(this.round.card.ready?.includes(p.id)?' / READY':''));h.text(32,198,'ENTER: READY    M: MORE TIME',{color:'sand'});if(ctx.input.wasPressed('Enter','PadCross'))this.options.session.answer('ready');if(ctx.input.wasPressed('KeyM','PadTriangle'))this.options.session.answer('more');}else h.text(24,18,'CASH RUN / FIND A CASE',{scale:2});}else{h.text(32,48,GAME_TITLE,{scale:4,color:'orange'});h.text(32,105,'A MAP IS A PROMISE.',{scale:2});h.text(32,171,this.notice||'ENTER / BEGIN',{scale:2});this.idle+=dt;}}\n roundEnded(){this.screen='results';this.ctx?.audio.stopMusic();this.ctx?.audio.stopLoops();}\n cameraTarget(){return this.pos;}\n eyePosition(){return this.eye.copy(this.pos).add(new THREE.Vector3(0,1.55,0));}\n onCameraChange(ctx){installLook(this,ctx);}\n state(){return {mode:this.mode,screen:this.screen,focus:this.focus,device:this.device,glyphSet:this.settings.glyphs,notice:this.notice,attract:this.mode==='attract',hp:this.hp,stones:this.stones,tablets:this.tablets,syrettes:this.syrettes,pos:this.pos.toArray(),hour:this.hour,wind:this.wind,prompts:this.prompts,round:this.round?{started:this.round.started,ended:this.round.ended,players:this.round.players,cases:this.round.cases}:null};}\n status(){return \"'`${this.mode} / ${this.screen||'\"'play'} / \"'${Math.round(this.hp)} HP`;}\n fingerprint(){return JSON.stringify(this.state());}\n dispose(){this.round?.dispose();}\n}\nexport const createGame=options=>new SorrelGame(options);\nEOF\ncat > src/main.js <<'\"'EOF'\nimport {Engine,withUrlOptions} from '../pixel-engine.js';\nimport {createGame} from './game.js';\nimport {LOOK} from './core/look.js';\nimport {hubSession} from './net/session.js';\nconst hub=globalThis.AIHub;\nlet info=null;\nif(hub?.active)info=await hub.connect({mode:'shared-world',seats:[1,4],card:true});\nconst touch=typeof matchMedia\"'!=='\"'undefined'&&matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches&&\"'!matchMedia('\"'(any-pointer: fine)').matches;\nconst game=createGame({session:info?hubSession(info):null,touch});\nconst OPTIONS=withUrlOptions({container:document.getElementById('app'),camera:{preset:'first',fov:68},look:LOOK,touch:false,debugKeys:false,settings:{button:false,key:false},seed:info?.seed??7341});\ntry {\n if(info?.server){const e=await Engine.headless(game,OPTIONS);window.__PIXEL_ENGINE__=e;window.__PIXEL_READY__=Promise.resolve(e);const timer=setInterval(()=>{if(game.round?.ended){clearInterval(timer);return;}e.step(6,1/60);},100);window.addEventListener('pagehide',()=>clearInterval(timer),{once:true});}\n else if(\"'!navigator.gpu){const root=document.getElementById('\"'app');root.className='fallback';root.innerHTML='<h1>HARDLY FAR CRY</h1><div>Controller or keyboard required</div><div>This browser cannot render the WebGPU world.<br>Open this file in a browser with WebGPU enabled.</div><button type=\\\"button\\\">SETTINGS / COMPATIBILITY</button>';root.querySelector('button').onclick=()=>root.querySelector('button').textContent='WEBGPU REQUIRED / CHROME OR EDGE';window.__GAME__=game;if(info)hub.fail('This game needs WebGPU');}\n else await Engine.start(game,OPTIONS);\n}catch(e){if(info)hub.fail(String(e.message||e));throw e;}\nif(info&&\"'!info.server){const answer=e=>{if(game.round?.ended||game.round?.started)return;if(e.code==='\"'Enter')hub.answer('ready');if(e.code==='KeyM')hub.answer('more');};window.addEventListener('keydown',answer);window.addEventListener('pagehide',()=>window.removeEventListener('keydown',answer),{once:true});}\nEOF\ncat > tests/run.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport {createHash} from 'node:crypto';\nimport {readFile,writeFile,readdir} from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport {resolve} from 'node:path';\nprocess.chdir(new URL('..',import.meta.url).pathname);\nconst args=process.argv.slice(2),only=args.includes('--only')?args[args.indexOf('--only')+1]:null;\nconst suiteNames=(await readdir('tests/suites')).filter(f=>f.endsWith('.mjs')).map(f=>f.slice(0,-4));\nlet stamps={};try{stamps=JSON.parse(await readFile('tests/.stamps.json','utf8'));}catch{}\nlet passed=0,failed=0,skipped=0;\nfor(const name of suiteNames){if(only&&name\"'!==only)continue;const suite=await import('\"'./suites/'+name+'.mjs');const files=suite.covers||[];const h=createHash('sha256');for(const f of files){try{h.update(await readFile(f));}catch{h.update(f);}}h.update(await readFile('tests/suites/'+name+'.mjs'));const digest=h.digest('hex');if(\"'!args.includes('\"'--all')&&\"'!only&&stamps[name]===digest){skipped++;continue;}const check=(ok,msg)=>{if(ok)passed++;else{failed++;console.error('\"'FAIL '+name+': '+msg);}};try{await suite.run(check);}catch(e){failed++;console.error('FAIL '+name+': '+e.stack);}if(failed===0)stamps[name]=digest;}\nawait writeFile('tests/.stamps.json',JSON.stringify(stamps,null,2));console.log(\"'`${passed} passed, ${failed} failed, ${skipped} suites unchanged`);process.exitCode=failed?1:0;\nEOF\ncat > tests/suites/hub.mjs <<'\"'EOF'\nimport {chromium} from 'playwright';\nimport {readFile,mkdir,copyFile,cp} from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport {createServer} from 'node:http';\nimport {resolve} from 'node:path';\nexport const covers=['src/net/round.js','src/net/session.js','src/main.js','src/game.js','index.html'];\nexport async function run(check){await mkdir('tests/.site',{recursive:true});await cp('vendor/hub','tests/.site',{recursive:true});await copyFile('../Hardly-Far-Cry-Far-Cry-2-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261105-063014.html','tests/.site/game.html');const root=resolve('tests/.site');const server=createServer(async(req,res)=>{try{const p=resolve(root,'.'+new URL(req.url,'http://local').pathname);if(\"'!p.startsWith(root+'\"'/'))throw Error('path');res.setHeader('Content-Type',p.endsWith('.js')?'application/javascript':'text/html');res.end(await readFile(p));}catch{res.writeHead(404).end();}});await new Promise(r=>server.listen(0,'127.0.0.1',r));const base='http://127.0.0.1:'+server.address().port;const browser=await chromium.launch({headless:true,args:['--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-angle=swiftshader','--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader']});\ntry{const ctx=await browser.newContext({viewport:{width:1280,height:720}});for(const query of ['players=2&auto=1','players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1','players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&scenario=host-leave','players=2&auto=1&scenario=server']){const page=await ctx.newPage();await page.goto(base+'/harness.html?game=game.html&'+query);await page.waitForFunction(()=>document.body.dataset.complete==='true',{},{timeout:150000});const r=await page.evaluate(()=>window.__hubCheck);check(r.pass,query+' '+JSON.stringify(r.checks.filter(c=>c.pass===false||c.ok===false)));await page.close();}await ctx.close();}finally{await browser.close();await new Promise(r=>server.close(r));}}\nEOF\ncat > tests/ISSUES.md <<'EOF'\n# Issues caught by testing\n\nEach numbered entry records a distinct defect discovered by a test, its severity, and its resolution.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs && node tests/run.mjs --only hub\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
