{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_64","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '4486,4538p' API.md && sed -n '2770,2788p' API.md && viewport-matrix --help | head -50\"","aggregated_output":"### class NavGrid\n\n- `new NavGrid(width: number, height: number, o: NavGridOptions = {})`\n- `static fromRows(rows: readonly string[], o: NavGridOptions & { blocked?: string } = {}): NavGrid`: From an ASCII map: `blocked` characters are closed, everything else open. Default '# ': walls and pits (a ' ' has no floor in RoomKit's maps); past the end of a short row is a wall.\n- `readonly width: number`\n- `readonly height: number`\n- `readonly cell: number`\n- `readonly ox: number`: World x, z of cell (0, 0)'s corner.\n- `readonly oz: number`\n- `readonly open: Uint8Array`: 1 = walkable.\n- `version: number`: Bumped by `setOpen`: flow fields rebuild.\n- `flowBuilds: number`: How many times a flow field was built (tools: should be one per target cell change).\n- `col(x: number): number`\n- `row(z: number): number`\n- `centerX(col: number): number`: World x, z of a cell's centre.\n- `centerZ(row: number): number`\n- `isOpen(col: number, row: number): boolean`\n- `walkable(x: number, z: number): boolean`: Is the world point on a walkable cell?\n- `setOpen(col: number, row: number, open: boolean): void`\n- `path(from: readonly [number, number, number], to: readonly [number, number, number]): [number, number, number][] | null`: Shortest path between two world points (x, z used; y kept from `from`): A* over cells, no corner cutting, then smoothed so it only turns where a wall is in the way. Null when there is no way. The first point is `from`, the last `to` (snapped into its cell).\n- `smooth(pts: [number, number, number][]): [number, number, number][]`: Drop every point the path can skip in a straight line.\n- `lineOfSight(ax: number, az: number, bx: number, bz: number, radius = 0): boolean`: Can you see (or walk straight) from a to b? Walks the cells under the segment (a DDA); `radius` > 0 also tests two lines offset sideways (a body that wide fits).\n- `castWall(ax: number, az: number, dx: number, dz: number, max: number): number`: Distance from a along a direction to the first closed cell (at most `max`): the same cell walk as `lineOfSight`, so a vision cone drawn with it shows exactly what a guard can see.\n- `flowTo(x: number, z: number): boolean`: A flow field toward the world point (x, z): the walking distance from every cell to it. Rebuilt only when the target changes cell or the grid changed (`version`). Returns whether it was rebuilt.\n- `flowDistance(x: number, z: number): number`: Walking distance to the flow target from a world point (Infinity: no way).\n- `flowDirection(x: number, z: number, out: [number, number]): boolean`: Which way to go from (x, z) toward the flow target: the unit direction to the lowest-distance neighbour (into `out` [x, z]). Returns false at the target or with no way.\n\n### interface NavGridOptions\n\nNavigation on a grid: which cells can be walked, the shortest path between two points\n(A*, 8-connected, no corner cutting, smoothed by line of sight), a flow field toward one\ntarget (one Dijkstra fill, then any number of agents read a direction per cell for free),\nand line-of-sight tests (vision cones, stealth). Pure and allocation-light; unit-tested.\n\n  const nav = NavGrid.fromRows(['#########', '#...#...#', '#.#...#.#', '#########'], { cell: 1, origin: [-4.5, 0, -2] });\n  const path = nav.path([-3, 0, -1], [3, 0, -1]);       // world points, corners only\n  nav.flowTo(hero.x, hero.z);                            // once when the target changes cell\n  nav.flowDirection(x, z, out);…\n\n- `cell?: number`: Metres per cell. Default 1.\n- `origin?: readonly [number, number, number]`: World x, z of the top-left cell's corner (column 0, row 0). Default: centred on the origin.\n\n### interface Noise\n\n- `readonly seed: number`\n- `n2(x: number, y: number): number`: Simplex noise in 2D, about -1..1.\n- `n3(x: number, y: number, z: number): number`: Simplex noise in 3D, about -1..1 (a 2D field that changes over time: n3(x, y, t)).\n- `fbm2(x: number, y: number, o?: FbmOptions): number`: Fractal Brownian motion: octaves of 2D noise added up, normalised to about -1..1.\n- `ridged2(x: number, y: number, o?: FbmOptions): number`: Ridged noise: 1 − |noise| per octave, squared, so creases become sharp crests; 0..1.\n\n### type Pattern\n\n```ts\n(clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\nresolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\n\n  ctx.hud.clear();\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\n\n- `new Hud(container: HTMLElement | null)`\n- `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`: The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn).\n- `visible: boolean`\n- `get width: number`: HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution).\n- `get height: number`\n- `text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation).\n- `rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor: HudAnchor = 'top-left'): void`: A filled rectangle (panels, bars).\n- `sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = transparent).\n- `clear(): void`: Remove everything.\n- `measure(text: string, scale = 1): { width: number; height: number }`: Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`.\n- `sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void`: Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed.\n- `dispose(): void`\nusage: viewport-matrix [-h] [-o OUT] [--engines ENGINES] [--all-engines]\n                       [--only ONLY] [--devices DEVICES] [--full-page]\n                       [--dpr1] [--wait WAIT] [--timeout TIMEOUT] [--headed]\n                       url\n\nScreenshot a URL across phone / foldable / tablet / desktop viewports in Chromium, WebKit and Firefox.\n\nWrites one PNG per (device, engine) plus index.html (contact sheet drawn to relative scale) and\nreport.json, and flags horizontal overflow, console errors, page errors and failed requests.\n\nBy default each device runs on the engine it really ships with (iPhone/iPad -> WebKit,\nAndroid -> Chromium) and desktop sizes run on all three engines.\n\n  viewport-matrix http://localhost:5173\n  viewport-matrix http://localhost:5173/play -o /tmp/shots --full-page\n  viewport-matrix URL --engines firefox              # everything in Firefox\n  viewport-matrix URL --all-engines                  # every device x every engine\n  viewport-matrix URL --only phone,foldable --dpr1   # small files, mobile only\n\npositional arguments:\n  url\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help         show this help message and exit\n  -o, --out OUT      output dir (default: $TMPDIR/viewport-matrix/<timestamp>)\n  --engines ENGINES  comma list from chromium,webkit,firefox\n  --all-engines      run every device on every selected engine\n  --only ONLY        comma list of categories: phone,foldable,tablet,desktop\n  --devices DEVICES  comma list of Playwright device names to use instead of\n                     the built-in matrix\n  --full-page        capture the whole scrollable page, not just the viewport\n  --dpr1             force device pixel ratio 1 (smaller PNGs)\n  --wait WAIT        extra ms to wait after load for animations (default 800)\n  --timeout TIMEOUT  navigation timeout in seconds (default 45)\n  --headed           show the browser windows\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"agent_message","text":"The systems suite now passes all 70 checks. The campaign bot has reached the mine after completing the earlier contracts, including the water bypass and buddy loss. Cash Run setup now takes about 1.6 seconds in headless tests; I’m checking the four-player hub deadline and both endings next."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_66","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Integrated game checkpoint\n- Replaced src/game.js with the complete composition of world, player, combat, body, vehicles, map, mission, UI, dev, attract and sessions.\n- Added all M0-M9 + End missions as data; original dialogue, six notes, both ending cards, paged About, settings/glyphs, shop/locker/bed/rail, buddies and persistence.\n- \"'`static`: **148 passed**. `systems`: **70 passed** after fixing pause opening. Real Chromium engine check passed WebGPU with zero page/game/GPU errors, and title screenshot visually inspected (warm grass/fire at dusk).\n- Full playthrough currently advances through M6 and into M7; improving bot'\"'s shooting vantage points around physical cover. Earlier contract objectives, scripted jam, driving/repair, fire, payroll and bypass pass.\n- Full-scene hub check initially exceeded 20s readiness, and four-copy memory pressure caused one harness crash. Restricted rounds to the designed Cut/Ranger/P5 geometry, 23 soldiers, one extraction truck. Sample 5m terrain heights interpolated to 2.5m mesh, cached ground classes: round headless setup now ~1.56s (was ~5s). Recheck running.\n- tests/ISSUES.md currently has 8 fixed distinct issues. Critical: 1, 2, 3, 6, 7.\n- Required final naming, folders, tools and paths remain as above.\n\n## Remaining integration/polish and validation\n- Finish playthrough bot through both endings; test replay, browser keyboard/mouse/pad/touch, same-computer link; re-run all hub scenarios.\n- Confirm and polish first-person, map, night fire, surgery, dialogue, dev and ending screenshots using tests/capture.mjs; only title has been inspected so far.\n- Inspect responsive screenshots including small phone/tablet/ultrawide and WebKit fallback. viewport-matrix available; cheatsheet absent.\n- Make all dev toggles draw actual debug overlays; finish aim assist / native glyph coverage; implement surviving buddies at ending; ensure round cases/peers/soldiers snapshots render properly (recent net enhancements awaiting test).\n- Update About feedback from actual final results, write exact root exit-interview.json, DESIGNERS.md/README, final rebuild and all-suites command.\nEOF\ncat > tests/suites/replay.mjs <<'EOF'\nimport {Engine} from '../../pixel-engine.js';\nimport {createGame} from '../../src/game.js';\nexport const covers=['src/game.js','src/core/look.js','src/actors/actors.js','src/world/terrain.js','src/world/fire.js'];\nconst tap=(e,k,n=1)=>{e.input.setKey(k,true);e.step(n);e.input.setKey(k,false);e.step(2);};\nexport async function run(check){const e=await Engine.headless(createGame(),{camera:{preset:'first'},seed:7341,viewport:{width:1280,height:720,dpr:1},settings:{button:false,key:false}});try{tap(e,'Enter');tap(e,'Enter');tap(e,'KeyM');tap(e,'Enter');e.step(6);tap(e,'KeyH');e.step(75);const rec=e.recording(),fp=e.fingerprint(),gameFp=e.game.fingerprint();check(\"'!!rec&&rec.frames.length>80,'\"'mission segment recording exists');await e.replay(rec,()=>e.loadGame(createGame()));check(e.game.fingerprint()===gameFp,'mission simulation replays deterministically');check(e.fingerprint()===fp,'engine and physics fingerprint replay exactly');}finally{e.dispose();}}\nEOF\nnode tests/run.mjs --only replay\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
