s`. The release zip in `vendor/` is the integrity reference. Run `node tools/build.mjs` after changes and the appropriate suite behind `node tests/run.mjs`.\n\n- **Sites:** add a record to `src/content/sites.js` with an id, name, x/z position, kind, radius and optional faction/guards. Kinds control dressing in `World.site`; existing kinds require no new code. Positions are metres, +x east, -z north, inside +/-640. Dev teleport and its coordinate readout help placement. Roads and river polylines are in `src/content/roads.js`.\n- **Weapons:** add a definition to `src/content/weapons.js`, including slot, magazine, reserve, rate, damage, range, wear and price. Add the matching procedural view definition in `src/art/viewmodels.js`. Buying unlocks clean copies. Systems read balance values live rather than copying them into cached values.\n- **Missions:** `src/content/missions.js` contains prerequisites, giver, pay, optional weather/hour/wind, alternate plan and steps. Supported objectives include goto, leave, use, deliver, collect, steal, report/talk, kill, destroy, burn, hold, ride, choice and named story scripts. Steps name a site or an interaction tag and supply their on-screen text. Add at least eight paired speaker/text lines in `src/content/dialogue.js`. Normal contracts appear automatically once their prerequisites resolve. Debug mission start bypasses prerequisites for authoring.\n- **Interaction objects:** `World.item` supplies a stable id, tag, verb, position, model, range and properties. Use existing tags for a normal case, bed, locker, crate, speaker, shop or delivery. Place explosive objectives with HP and `explosive:true` so they acquire fuel cells, accept bullets and chain through fire.\n- **People and scenery:** `src/art/models.js` exports plain native ModelDef objects and a catalog. Reuse a library prop or the person factory; palette slots must exist on the selected model. Run `node check.mjs --sheets src/art/models.js`, inspect the PNGs and run the static suite. `src/art/clips.js` and `src/art/viewmodels.js` hold 30fps native ClipDef data.\n- **Writing and sound:** use the native HUD character set and short sentences. Subtitles wrap to 58 characters. Notes and epigraphs are in the dialogue content file. Music is Song data in `src/audio/music.js`; effects are SoundDef data in `src/audio/sfx.js`. Animalese voices derive deterministic syllables from the text. Music defaults and resets to 0.1.\n- **Balance:** `src/content/tuning-defaults.js` defines the default, min, max and step for each live slider. The same table builds Dev Mode'\"'s Balance pages. Reset restores every value. Settings live in a separate storage key from the single versioned campaign save.\n\nKeep interactions reachable and missions completable through their real actions. Add a test of each new rule, update the scripted playthrough when story dependencies change, and record discovered defects in \"'`tests/ISSUES.md`. The game-state snapshot, status and fingerprint are public tooling interfaces. The multiplayer host owns health, soldiers, cases and fire; clients submit their own movement and action events, render local feedback immediately, and consume host snapshots. All session traffic passes through the session adapter.\nEOF\ncat > .gitignore <<'\"'EOF'\nnode_modules/\ncheck/\ntests/.site/\ntests/.captures/\ntests/.stamps.json\ntests/*.log\nEOF\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Validation and final polish checkpoint\n- Full campaign now passes both endings, with a permanently dead buddy: **25 passed**. Replay: **3 passed**, including exact engine/physics fingerprint. Systems: **70 passed**.\n- Final full-world hub readiness fix: show the card/terrain before revealing the full mine scene at the shared start; gameplay data is loaded before ready, net traffic has its own interval. All **4 hub scenarios now pass**.\n- Browser suite: **20 passed** (native keyboard/mouse, standard pad, Xbox prompts, Web Audio rendering, clean errors, phone tap Settings, attract and WebKit fallback). Link suite: **6 passed** with shared pickup, fire, bank and standings over two file pages.\n- Static suite now **150 passed**. Model sheets generated and inspected for acacia/soldier. Engine is still unmodified.\n- TV screenshots captured without page/game/GPU errors. Inspected title, day, night fire, held map at wheel, shop and dev sliders; tightened ammo/caption spacing, fixed map/controller prompts and cursor conflict. Latest source needs refreshed screenshots, final full test command and rebuilt deliverable.\n- \"'`tests/ISSUES.md`: 12 distinct fixed issues, 5 critical (1,2,3,6,7). Other exploratory/test-harness fixes classified noncritical.\n- README.md and DESIGNERS.md written. Wildlife is the only intentionally omitted optional system; no wildlife UI/traces ship.\n- Responsive viewport-matrix WebKit run started in its requested /tmp output folder (direct AGENTS.md output rule), all project/test code stays in the dev directory.\n\n## Final steps remaining\n1. Inspect remaining dialogue/surgery/ending screenshots plus responsive small phone/tablet/wide outputs; capture latest UI/build.\n2. Fill feedback arrays in src/content/about.js and exact root exit-interview.json using actual test results. Parse/validate JSON.\n3. Rebuild and run `node tests/run.mjs --all` on final code, maintaining 0 failures; update this log and provide root HTML + interview links with required Source/Testing/Engine/Prompt feedback in final response.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
