{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_116","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > game.js <<'EOF'\n// Compatibility entry point for the shipped engine checker.\n// The browser starts through src/main.js; the complete game is defined in src/game.js.\nexport {createGame,SorrelGame} from './src/game.js';\nEOF\npython3 - <<'PY'\np='tests/run.mjs';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"async function memoryWindow(){\\\", \\\"async function memoryWindow(name){\\\");s=s.replace(\\\"if(kb>4*1024*1024)return;\\\", \\\"if(kb>4*1024*1024)return;await writeFile('tests/live-status.json',JSON.stringify({suite:name,state:'waiting for shared-machine memory',availableMB:Math.round(kb/1024)}));\\\");s=s.replace(\\\"await memoryWindow();result=await worker(name)\\\", \\\"await memoryWindow(name);await writeFile('tests/live-status.json',JSON.stringify({suite:name,state:'running',attempt:attempt+1}));result=await worker(name)\\\");s=s.replace(\\\"await writeFile('tests/.stamps.json'\\\", \\\"await writeFile('tests/live-status.json',JSON.stringify({state:'complete',passed,failed,skipped}));await writeFile('tests/.stamps.json'\\\");open(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/capture.mjs';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"063014.html'));\\\", \\\"063014.html')+(process.argv.includes('--low')?'?quality=low':''));\\\");open(p,'w').write(s)\np='README.md';s=open(p).read();s+='\\\\nThe test command isolates suites in child processes, waits briefly for memory before browser work, and retries only infrastructure crashes. \"'`tests/results.json` records the final results. Capture can use `node tests/capture.mjs --low` on a crowded software-rendering host; the shipping default remains medium.'\"\\\\n';open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nnode tests/run.mjs --all\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_117","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nbase=Path('tests/.captures')\nold=base/'default-quality'\nold.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\nfor p in base.glob('*'):\n if p.is_file() and p.suffix in ['.png','.json']:shutil.copy2(p,old/p.name)\nPY\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Test-runner resilience\n- The last rerun encountered browser processes terminated by shared-host memory pressure (including launch itself); the headless gameplay checks still passed. No task-owned stale browser processes were present.\n- The test command now isolates every suite in its own child process, limits the Node heap, waits briefly for a memory window before browser work, and retries only infrastructure crashes. Failed assertions and protocol checks are never retried or hidden. \"'`tests/results.json` is the final report; `tests/live-status.json` shows the current suite.\n- A fresh final run is active under the most recent session id; expected 287 assertions. The prior successful full run was 285/0 before two extra regression assertions.\n- `game.js` now re-exports the real game for the kit checker. Default-quality screenshots were preserved under `tests/.captures/default-quality`; the final capture script supports `--low` for a crowded software-rendering host.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
